  "steps": [
    "Marinate the chicken. Mix the chipotle in adobo, taco seasoning, garlic powder, honey, lime juice, lime zest and salt. Add the chicken, toss to coat, and marinate at least 30 minutes.",
    "Corn salad. Husk the corn, spray lightly with oil, and season with taco seasoning. Cook in a large pan over medium-high heat 8–12 minutes, turning, until tender and charred. Slice off the kernels and toss with the pepper, onion, coriander, jalapeño, lime juice and salt.",
    "Cook the chicken. Preheat the air fryer to 200 °C for 5 minutes. Lay the chicken in one layer, pour over the marinade, cook 7–8 minutes, flip, then 6 more minutes until charred and cooked through. Rest 5 minutes, then slice. Or use a lightly oiled pan over medium-high heat.",
    "Guacamole. Mash the avocado until mostly smooth, then fold in the tomato, onion, coriander, garlic powder, lime juice and salt.",
    "Rice. Toss the cooked rice with the chopped coriander and lime zest.",
    "Assemble. Divide the rice between four bowls. Top with the sliced chicken, corn salad, guacamole, pickled onions and coriander."
  ],
